 on January 19, 1946, in Sevier County, Tennessee. She grew up in a humbleone-bedroom homein the Smoky Mountains of East Tennessee with her 11 brothers and sisters.Her musical talent was apparent from a young age. She wrote her first song at five with her mom transcribing the event because Dolly was not able to read or write yet. She moved to Nashville after high school graduation and was mentored by her songwriter uncle, Bill Owens.In 1967, her debut album,Hello, I’m Dolly, was released which contained the singles “Dumb Blonde” and “Something Fishy.” She toured on the Porter Wagoner Show for seven years before going out on her own.Her depar...", "published_at": "2026-09-25T14:01:00+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Fast Company", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://www.fastcompany.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 35, "sensationalism": 21, "opinion_fact": 32, "factual_rigor": 26, "framing": 31, "confidence": 0.53, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 50.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 0.0, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 50.0, "source_baseline": 35, "text_shift": 0.0, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": [], "framing_phrases_found": [], "entity_sentiments": {}, "state_affiliated": false, "unscored": false}, "sensationalism": {"headline_score": 5.0, "body_score": 11.6, "clickbait_signals": 0, "superlative_density": 0.0, "urgency_density": 0.0, "hyperbole_density": 0.0, "measured_density": 0.0, "partisan_attack_density": 0.0}, "opinion": {"pronoun_score": 0.0, "subjectivity_score": 41.4, "modal_score": 11.3, "hedging_score": 0.0, "attribution_score": 75.0, "metadata_score": 0.0, "value_judgment_score": 0.0, "absolutist_assertion_score": 0.0, "classification": "Analysis", "dominant_signals": ["attribution_gaps", "subjectivity", "modal_language"]}, "coverage": {"named_sources_count": 1, "org_citations_count": 0, "data_points_count": 0, "direct_quotes_count": 4, "vague_sources_cou